WEBVTT

00:18:29.796 --> 00:18:31.716
But one of the things you see widespread

00:18:31.756 --> 00:18:34.156
is that there are,
in the architecture of regret,

00:18:34.196 --> 00:18:36.436
there are often two kinds of regrets.

00:18:36.476 --> 00:18:39.716
One are regrets of action
and one are regrets of inaction.

00:18:39.716 --> 00:18:41.236
Regrets about what we did.

00:18:41.276 --> 00:18:42.836
Regrets about what we didn't do.

00:18:42.836 --> 00:18:45.596
And overwhelmingly,
inaction regrets predominate.

00:18:45.636 --> 00:18:47.756
And that's what an opportunity lost is.

00:18:48.316 --> 00:18:49.916
With action regrets,

00:18:49.916 --> 00:18:53.476
we can try to undo them.

00:18:53.476 --> 00:18:55.076
We can make amends.

00:18:55.116 --> 00:18:58.076
We can look for the silver lining,
and we can reduce the sting.

00:18:58.076 --> 00:19:00.516
For inaction regrets, it is harder.